{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.DemandStability","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.DemandStability","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Interactions.DerivedAtom","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Module"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.mixed_crossing_square_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.mixed_crossing_square_identity","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DemandStability.lean#L127-L149","doc":"The mixed crossing square: (2σ - HA)² = 4 + HA².\nUses the Hecke relation σ² = HA·σ + 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.typed_crossing_square_pp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.typed_crossing_square_pp","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/DemandStability.lean#L104-L114","doc":"The typed crossing squares reduce via the Hecke relation.\nThis is the key identity for polynomial scaling of the\ninductive GB reduction.\n\nC_pp² = HA · C_pp + 1\nC_nn² = HA · C_nn + 1  (after expanding σ⁻¹ = σ - HA)\n\nBoth are instances of σ² = HA·σ + 1. ","signatureChunk":0}]}